{
  "_about": [
    "Hand-authored muscle labels for every library exercise, keyed by id. merge.mjs fails if an exercise is missing, a name does not match its id, or a region id is not in src/lib/muscleRegions.ts.",
    "primary = the prime movers only: the muscles that move the joints under load (counts 1 hard set). secondary = meaningful helpers (counts 0.5). Anything smaller is left out.",
    "Where docs/research/workout-mode/evidence.json has a kept claim about an exercise, the labels agree with it: squats and the leg press list no rectus femoris, hamstrings or side glutes (MRI found little or no growth there); the seated calf raise lists no gastrocnemius; the triceps exercises list all three heads; lunges, split squats and step-ups list the vasti and glute max as main, with the side glutes and adductors helping, and no rectus femoris (lunge EMG ranked it below the glutes); overhead presses list the triceps as main with the upper chest and upper traps helping (overhead-press-anatomy).",
    "Cardio exercises (type cardio) get mode cardio and no regions. Mode: weighted = a weight is required; bodyweight/band/timed = no weight needed."
  ],

